hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1131","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala narrated to us, saying: Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reported this. He said: “Satan ties three knots on the back of one of you’s heads when he sleeps. Every knot he ties, he says: You have a long night. If he wakes up and remembers God, one knot will be untied, and if he performs ablution, two knots will be untied. He prayed, and the knots were untied, so he became active and had a good soul. Otherwise, he became evil and lazy.” This is the wording of the hadith of Al-Dourqi."
